WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.751
Stable imagery is essential.

00:00:01.751 --> 00:00:05.054
Wind, vibration, rapid movement, poor focus, glare, haze,

00:00:05.054 --> 00:00:09.183
and motion blur can hide defects or create false features.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:14.963
Pause or repeat a safe capture instead of completing the route with unusable data.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.440
Use overview, intermediate, and close-up views.

00:00:17.440 --> 00:00:20.743
The overview establishes the asset and component location.

00:00:20.743 --> 00:00:22.807
Intermediate views connect local geometry.

00:00:22.807 --> 00:00:24.459
Close-ups show the feature.

00:00:24.459 --> 00:00:29.000
This sequence prevents a detailed image from becoming an orphaned finding.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.890
Overlap supports mapping, stitching, and complete coverage.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.019
Consistent route, angle, distance, speed, and capture interval improve repeatability.

00:00:36.019 --> 00:00:40.560
Avoid gaps around edges, joints, undersides, transitions, or other scoped components.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:45.101
Scale context helps reviewers estimate size, but perspective can distort dimensions.

00:00:45.101 --> 00:00:50.056
Use approved references, known asset geometry, or calibrated methods where measurement matters.

00:00:50.056 --> 00:00:53.771
Do not estimate defect size from an arbitrary screenshot.

00:00:53.771 --> 00:00:57.900
Repeatable routes support trend analysis, yet construction, vegetation, access, weather,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:00:59.139
and equipment change.

00:00:59.139 --> 00:01:05.331
Preserve route version and deviations so differences in viewpoint are not mistaken for asset deterioration.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:09.873
Record date, time, asset, component, location confidence, aircraft, sensor, settings, weather,

00:01:09.873 --> 00:01:13.176
lighting, load state where relevant, and source file.

00:01:13.176 --> 00:01:19.369
Review a sample during the mission when safe so missing coverage is caught before demobilization.

00:01:19.369 --> 00:01:23.497
Maintain a coverage log or annotated asset plan during collection.

00:01:23.497 --> 00:01:25.149
Mark completed, incomplete, obstructed,

00:01:25.149 --> 00:01:30.103
and deferred areas so the team can distinguish an inspected component from

00:01:30.103 --> 00:01:32.580
one that simply produced no image.
